# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate carries the time evolution $e^{-itH}$ of a whole operator. A fermion-to-fermion synthesis rewrites that gate into a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") of smaller fermionic gates. Both sides of the rewrite stay in fermionic space, which is what distinguishes it from the fermion-to-qubit synthesis that follows: the operator’s [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") (see [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)) survive it, whereas a fermion-to-qubit mapping returns a [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), which has no concept of grouping.\n"
msgstr "Gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") membawa evolusi masa $e^{-itH}$ bagi keseluruhan operator. Sintesis fermion-ke-fermion menulis semula Gate itu menjadi [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") yang terdiri daripada Gate fermionik yang lebih kecil. Kedua-dua belah penulisan semula kekal dalam ruang fermionik, dan inilah yang membezakannya daripada sintesis fermion-ke-qubit yang menyusul: [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") operator (lihat [Kumpulkan sebutan operator: gunakan struktur operator](grouping#grouping-explanation)) kekal selepasnya, manakala pemetaan fermion-ke-qubit mengembalikan [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), yang tidak mempunyai konsep pengumpulan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two knobs select the method. `Evolution.synthesis` sets it on one gate, and the [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") transpiler pass sets it across a whole circuit. Both take an [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\"), the interface any such rewrite implements. The methods this package currently provides for an evolution are product formulas, which is what the rest of this guide uses: [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") for a first-order formula (the default) and [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") for a higher even order. Anything else implementing the interface is selected the same way, and the sections on the two knobs apply to it unchanged.\n"
msgstr "Dua kenop memilih kaedah. `Evolution.synthesis` menetapkannya pada satu Gate, dan laluan Transpiler [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") menetapkannya pada keseluruhan litar. Kedua-duanya menerima [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\"), iaitu antara muka yang dilaksanakan oleh sebarang penulisan semula sedemikian. Kaedah yang disediakan pakej ini pada masa ini untuk evolusi ialah formula hasil darab, yang digunakan oleh bahagian panduan selebihnya: [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") untuk formula peringkat pertama (lalai) dan [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") untuk peringkat genap yang lebih tinggi. Apa-apa lagi yang melaksanakan antara muka ini dipilih dengan cara yang sama, dan bahagian tentang kedua-dua kenop itu terpakai kepadanya tanpa perubahan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  This fermion-to-fermion step is **optional**. An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate can go straight to the fermion-to-qubit stage, which maps and synthesizes it whole however many terms it holds. Splitting it first is a choice, made because the resulting gates are individually cheaper or because the split exposes structure that a later stage can use.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Langkah fermion-ke-fermion ini adalah **pilihan**. Gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") boleh terus ke peringkat fermion-ke-qubit, yang memetakan dan mensintesisnya secara keseluruhan tanpa mengira bilangan sebutan yang dipegangnya. Memecahkannya terlebih dahulu ialah satu pilihan, dibuat kerana Gate yang terhasil setiap satunya lebih murah atau kerana pemecahan itu mendedahkan struktur yang dapat digunakan oleh peringkat kemudian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The two steps compose, so an evolution can end up approximated at either level, at both, or at neither. A product formula approximates unless its factors commute; a synthesis method need not approximate at all.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Kedua-dua langkah ini boleh digubah, jadi evolusi boleh berakhir dianggarkan pada salah satu peringkat, pada kedua-duanya, atau pada kedua-duanya tidak. Formula hasil darab membuat anggaran kecuali faktornya berkomut; kaedah sintesis tidak semestinya membuat anggaran sama sekali.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Skipping this step does not have to mean losing the grouping entirely. Wrapping the mapper in [`group_wise()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-group-wise#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise\") maps the operator one group at a time and sums the results, so the mapped Pauli terms arrive grouped rather than interleaved. A qubit-side product formula synthesizes them in the order it receives, so commuting terms that end up adjacent can be scheduled together.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Melangkau langkah ini tidak semestinya bermakna kehilangan pengumpulan sepenuhnya. Membungkus pemeta dengan [`group_wise()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-group-wise#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise\") memetakan operator satu kumpulan pada satu masa dan menjumlahkan hasilnya, supaya sebutan Pauli yang dipetakan tiba secara berkumpulan dan bukannya bersilang-selang. Formula hasil darab sebelah qubit mensintesisnya mengikut turutan yang diterimanya, jadi sebutan berkomut yang akhirnya bersebelahan boleh dijadualkan bersama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  On the Hamiltonian below that recovers the whole two-qubit depth benefit of splitting: 18 instead of 30, at an unchanged gate count. The difference is *where* the structure is expressed. Splitting in fermionic space makes each group a separate gate, which every later stage can see and act on; `group_wise` leaves one gate and only reorders the terms inside it, which is enough for scheduling but leaves nothing for a fermionic pass to work with. Use it when the evolution has to stay a single gate, and reach for a fermionic product formula otherwise.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Pada Hamiltonian di bawah, itu memulihkan keseluruhan faedah kedalaman dua-qubit hasil pemecahan: 18 berbanding 30, dengan bilangan Gate yang tidak berubah. Perbezaannya ialah *di mana* struktur itu dinyatakan. Memecahkan dalam ruang fermionik menjadikan setiap kumpulan satu Gate yang berasingan, yang dapat dilihat dan digunakan oleh setiap peringkat kemudian; `group_wise` meninggalkan satu Gate dan hanya menyusun semula sebutan di dalamnya, yang memadai untuk penjadualan tetapi tidak meninggalkan apa-apa untuk dikerjakan oleh laluan fermionik. Gunakannya apabila evolusi mesti kekal sebagai satu Gate, dan gunakan formula hasil darab fermionik jika tidak.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a grouped Hamiltonian {#build-a-grouped-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Bina Hamiltonian berkumpulan {#build-a-grouped-hamiltonian}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both product formulas split an operator into factors, and for a grouped operator those factors are its groups. The grouping is therefore what determines both the cost and the accuracy of the result. Take a six-site Fermi-Hubbard chain, grouped the way its terms commute: the hopping terms on even bonds, the hopping terms on odd bonds, and the diagonal interaction.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua formula hasil darab memecahkan operator kepada faktor, dan bagi operator berkumpulan faktor tersebut ialah kumpulannya. Oleh itu pengumpulan menentukan kos dan ketepatan hasilnya. Ambil rantai Fermi-Hubbard enam tapak, dikumpulkan mengikut cara sebutannya berkomut: sebutan lompatan pada ikatan genap, sebutan lompatan pada ikatan ganjil, dan interaksi pepenjuru.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fifteen terms in three groups. Each hopping group pairs every term with its conjugate partner, which matters: a factor has to be Hermitian for its exponential to be unitary, and that does not follow from the sum being Hermitian. [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") checks that convention rather than leaving it to inspection:\n"
msgstr "Lima belas sebutan dalam tiga kumpulan. Setiap kumpulan lompatan memasangkan setiap sebutan dengan pasangan konjugatnya, yang penting: faktor mesti Hermitian supaya eksponennya unitari, dan itu tidak terhasil daripada hakikat bahawa jumlahnya Hermitian. [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") menyemak konvensyen itu dan bukannya membiarkannya kepada pemeriksaan visual:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Separating $a^\\dagger_0 a_1$ from its partner $a^\\dagger_1 a_0$ would break it, and leaving the operator ungrouped has the same effect, since both formulas then split it *term by term* and a lone $a^\\dagger_i a_j$ is not Hermitian:\n"
msgstr "Memisahkan $a^\\dagger_0 a_1$ daripada pasangannya $a^\\dagger_1 a_0$ akan merosakkannya, dan membiarkan operator tidak berkumpulan mempunyai kesan yang sama, kerana kedua-dua formula kemudian memecahkannya *sebutan demi sebutan* dan $a^\\dagger_i a_j$ yang tunggal tidak Hermitian:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Such a factor is a valid fermionic operator, and this package will build the gate for it, so nothing complains until the mapped operator reaches [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), which requires real coefficients and raises `ValueError: Operator contains complex coefficients, which are not supported`. Checking the grouping up front turns that late failure into an answer available before any circuit is built.\n"
msgstr "Faktor sedemikian ialah operator fermionik yang sah, dan pakej ini akan membina Gate untuknya, jadi tiada apa yang merungut sehingga operator yang dipetakan sampai kepada [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), yang memerlukan pekali nyata dan menimbulkan `ValueError: Operator contains complex coefficients, which are not supported`. Menyemak pengumpulan lebih awal menukarkan kegagalan lewat itu menjadi jawapan yang tersedia sebelum sebarang litar dibina.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the method on one gate {#set-the-method-on-one-gate}"
msgstr "Tetapkan kaedah pada satu Gate {#set-the-method-on-one-gate}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass a synthesis method to the gate, then decompose it. Each gate it emits comes back as its own [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate:\n"
msgstr "Lulus kaedah sintesis kepada Gate, kemudian uraikannya. Setiap Gate yang dikeluarkannya kembali sebagai Gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") tersendiri:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First order emits one factor per group. Order two emits the symmetric palindrome, so the two outer groups appear twice at half the time each, giving five. Four repetitions of that would give twenty, but each repetition ends on the same group the next one begins with. Those neighboring gates evolve under the same operator, so they are fused into one gate with the summed time, which saves one gate per seam. Pass `merge_adjacent=False` to keep the textbook sequence. Every order splits the operator the same way; what changes is the ordering of the factors and their evolution times, not the partition.\n"
msgstr "Peringkat pertama mengeluarkan satu faktor bagi setiap kumpulan. Peringkat kedua mengeluarkan palindrom simetri, jadi dua kumpulan luar muncul dua kali pada separuh masa masing-masing, menjadikannya lima. Empat ulangan itu akan memberikan dua puluh, tetapi setiap ulangan berakhir pada kumpulan yang sama dengan permulaan ulangan berikutnya. Gate bersebelahan itu berevolusi di bawah operator yang sama, jadi ia digabungkan menjadi satu Gate dengan masa terjumlah, yang menjimatkan satu Gate bagi setiap sambungan. Lulus `merge_adjacent=False` untuk mengekalkan jujukan buku teks. Setiap peringkat memecahkan operator dengan cara yang sama; yang berubah ialah susunan faktor dan masa evolusinya, bukan pembahagiannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The factors are marked `atomic`, so decomposing again leaves them in place rather than splitting them further. The decomposition has a fixed point, which is what makes it safe to call [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose\") repeatedly.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Faktor tersebut ditandakan `atomic`, jadi menguraikan semula membiarkannya di tempatnya dan bukannya memecahkannya lagi. Penguraian mempunyai titik tetap, yang menjadikannya selamat untuk memanggil [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose\") berulang kali.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the method for a whole pipeline {#set-the-method-for-a-whole-pipeline}"
msgstr "Tetapkan kaedah untuk keseluruhan saluran paip {#set-the-method-for-a-whole-pipeline}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting `synthesis` per gate means threading the choice through everything that builds one, including [`UCC`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucc#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC\") and [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\"), which construct their gates internally. The [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") pass applies one method to every [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") in a circuit instead, so the choice is made once for the pipeline. It is configured by gate name, the same way [`F2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis\") is, and a gate that is not named is left as it is:\n"
msgstr "Menetapkan `synthesis` bagi setiap Gate bermakna menyalurkan pilihan melalui segala yang membinanya, termasuk [`UCC`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucc#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC\") dan [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\"), yang membina Gate mereka secara dalaman. Laluan [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") sebaliknya menerapkan satu kaedah pada setiap [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") dalam litar, jadi pilihan dibuat sekali untuk saluran paip. Ia dikonfigurasikan mengikut nama Gate, sama seperti [`F2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis\"), dan Gate yang tidak dinamakan dibiarkan seperti sedia ada:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the same count [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose\") gives for that method above. The [`MergeEvolutions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-evolutions#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeEvolutions \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeEvolutions\") pass applies the same fusion to neighboring gates that did not come from one synthesis, such as the seams between consecutive circuits. The pass carries the formula out itself, so no separate expansion step is needed, and running it twice changes nothing, since the factors it emits are `atomic` and so carry no definition of their own.\n"
msgstr "Ini ialah bilangan yang sama yang diberikan oleh [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose\") untuk kaedah itu di atas. Laluan [`MergeEvolutions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-evolutions#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeEvolutions \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeEvolutions\") menerapkan penggabungan yang sama pada Gate bersebelahan yang tidak datang daripada satu sintesis, seperti sambungan antara litar berturutan. Laluan ini melaksanakan formula itu sendiri, jadi tiada langkah pengembangan berasingan diperlukan, dan menjalankannya dua kali tidak mengubah apa-apa, kerana faktor yang dikeluarkannya ialah `atomic` dan oleh itu tidak membawa takrifan tersendiri.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Note\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Note\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Pass `apply=False` to only *select* the method and leave the expansion to something else, such as Qiskit’s [`Decompose`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.Decompose) (naming the gate as `Decompose(\"Evolution\")` restricts it to the evolutions, leaving the other fermionic gates to their own synthesis plugins).\n"
msgstr "  Lulus `apply=False` untuk hanya *memilih* kaedah dan menyerahkan pengembangan kepada sesuatu yang lain, seperti [`Decompose`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.Decompose) Qiskit (menamakan Gate sebagai `Decompose(\"Evolution\")` mengehadkannya kepada evolusi, membiarkan Gate fermionik lain kepada pemalam sintesis masing-masing).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  This is useful to choose the method for a whole circuit up front while deferring the expansion to the point where it is wanted, for example to inspect the circuit first:\n"
msgstr "  Ini berguna untuk memilih kaedah bagi keseluruhan litar terlebih dahulu sambil menangguhkan pengembangan ke titik apabila ia dikehendaki, contohnya untuk memeriksa litar dahulu:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Be aware of what an unexpanded gate does, though: it reaches the fermion-to-qubit stage whole, where it is mapped without `synthesis` being consulted. That makes for an easy mistake when comparing methods, because every one of them then produces identical output and the comparison silently measures nothing. On the Hamiltonian above, leaving the order-two gate unexpanded collapses the much larger circuit below to the cost of a single mapped evolution, no matter which method was selected.\n"
msgstr "  Namun, ketahui apa yang dilakukan oleh Gate yang tidak dikembangkan: ia sampai ke peringkat fermion-ke-qubit secara keseluruhan, di mana ia dipetakan tanpa `synthesis` dirujuk. Itu mudah menyebabkan kesilapan semasa membandingkan kaedah, kerana setiap satunya kemudian menghasilkan output yang sama dan perbandingan secara senyap tidak mengukur apa-apa. Pada Hamiltonian di atas, membiarkan Gate peringkat kedua tidak dikembangkan meruntuhkan litar yang jauh lebih besar di bawah kepada kos satu evolusi terpeta, tanpa mengira kaedah yang dipilih.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure the payoff {#measure-the-payoff}"
msgstr "Ukur manfaatnya {#measure-the-payoff}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A higher order costs depth, so the question is not whether it is more accurate but whether it is more accurate *per gate*. Two numbers are needed per method: the error of the state it produces, and the two-qubit cost of the circuit that produced it.\n"
msgstr "Peringkat yang lebih tinggi memerlukan kedalaman, jadi persoalannya bukan sama ada ia lebih tepat tetapi sama ada ia lebih tepat *bagi setiap Gate*. Dua nombor diperlukan bagi setiap kaedah: ralat keadaan yang dihasilkannya, dan kos dua-qubit litar yang menghasilkannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The error is measured with [ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/), which simulates a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") **directly** (see [How this package relates to ffsim](ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation)). No fermion-to-qubit mapping is involved, so the comparison isolates the fermionic product formula from anything the mapping or the qubit-side synthesis might contribute. It also works in the fixed-particle-number sector, which is both smaller than the full $2^N$ space and the space the evolution actually stays in.\n"
msgstr "Ralat diukur dengan [ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/), yang mensimulasikan [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") **secara langsung** (lihat [Bagaimana pakej ini berkaitan dengan ffsim](ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation)). Tiada pemetaan fermion-ke-qubit terlibat, jadi perbandingan ini mengasingkan formula hasil darab fermionik daripada apa-apa yang mungkin disumbangkan oleh pemetaan atau sintesis sebelah qubit. Ia juga berfungsi dalam sektor bilangan zarah tetap, yang lebih kecil daripada ruang penuh $2^N$ dan merupakan ruang yang sebenarnya diduduki oleh evolusi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two-qubit cost is left out of that table on purpose. It depends on the qubit-side synthesis Qiskit selects, which improves between releases, so the numbers printed here would be a snapshot rather than a property of the product formula. The figure below plots them instead, and what the comparison rests on is asserted as a relation:\n"
msgstr "Kos dua-qubit sengaja ditinggalkan daripada jadual itu. Ia bergantung pada sintesis sebelah qubit yang dipilih Qiskit, yang bertambah baik antara keluaran, jadi nombor yang dicetak di sini hanya akan menjadi petikan sesaat dan bukan sifat formula hasil darab. Rajah di bawah memplotkannya sebaliknya, dan apa yang menjadi asas perbandingan dinyatakan sebagai hubungan:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Grouped bars of CX count and depth per method, with order two at four repetitions clearly shorter than order one at ten.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/fermionic_synthesis-8.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Grouped bars of CX count and depth per method, with order two at four repetitions clearly shorter than order one at ten.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/fermionic_synthesis-8.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the last two methods together, because they are the comparison that matters. Order two with four repetitions is roughly ten times more accurate than order one with ten, and it gets there with fewer entangling gates rather than more, as the figure shows. Spending a gate budget on a higher order beats spending it on more first-order steps here.\n"
msgstr "Baca dua kaedah terakhir bersama, kerana itulah perbandingan yang penting. Peringkat dua dengan empat ulangan kira-kira sepuluh kali lebih tepat daripada peringkat satu dengan sepuluh, dan ia mencapainya dengan lebih sedikit Gate berbelit dan bukan lebih banyak, seperti yang ditunjukkan oleh rajah. Membelanjakan bajet Gate pada peringkat yang lebih tinggi mengatasi membelanjakannya pada lebih banyak langkah peringkat pertama di sini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That result is not universal. Increasing [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.reps\") and increasing [`order`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.order \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.order\") reduce the error at different rates for the same kind of cost, and which wins depends on the operator and on the time being evolved. The two rows above are how to find out for a given problem.\n"
msgstr "Keputusan itu tidak universal. Meningkatkan [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.reps\") dan meningkatkan [`order`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.order \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.order\") mengurangkan ralat pada kadar yang berbeza bagi jenis kos yang sama, dan yang mana menang bergantung pada operator dan masa yang dievolusikan. Dua baris di atas ialah cara untuk mengetahuinya bagi sesuatu masalah tertentu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The fermionic formula composes with the one chosen for the fermion-to-qubit stage (see [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\")). Where both approximate, the accuracy of the result is governed by the weaker of the two, so raising the order here while the qubit-side formula stays first-order buys little.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Formula fermionik tergubah dengan formula yang dipilih untuk peringkat fermion-ke-qubit (lihat [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\")). Apabila kedua-duanya menganggar, ketepatan hasil ditentukan oleh yang lebih lemah antara keduanya, jadi menaikkan peringkat di sini sementara formula sebelah qubit kekal peringkat pertama memberikan sedikit manfaat.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Restrict the pass to the gates that benefit {#restrict-the-pass-to-the-gates-that-benefit}"
msgstr "Hadkan laluan kepada Gate yang mendapat manfaat {#restrict-the-pass-to-the-gates-that-benefit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A higher order only helps when the factors do not commute. If they all commute, the first-order formula is already exact and the extra factors are pure overhead. A purely diagonal operator makes that concrete, since number operators commute with each other:\n"
msgstr "Peringkat yang lebih tinggi hanya membantu apabila faktor tidak berkomut. Jika semuanya berkomut, formula peringkat pertama sudah tepat dan faktor tambahan hanyalah overhed semata-mata. Operator pepenjuru sepenuhnya menjadikannya nyata, kerana operator nombor berkomut sesama sendiri:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both circuits are exact, so the second spends 80% more entangling gates for nothing. The diagonal Coulomb operators of a [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") have this shape, which is why [`F2FSynthesis.filter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis.filter \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis.filter\") exists: it takes a predicate over the [`DAGOpNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.dagcircuit.DAGOpNode) and leaves the rejected gates untouched, so one pass can raise the order on the gates that benefit and leave the rest at first order.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua litar tepat, jadi yang kedua membelanjakan 80% lebih banyak Gate berbelit tanpa faedah. Operator Coulomb pepenjuru bagi [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") mempunyai bentuk ini, itulah sebabnya [`F2FSynthesis.filter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis.filter \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis.filter\") wujud: ia mengambil predikat ke atas [`DAGOpNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.dagcircuit.DAGOpNode) dan membiarkan Gate yang ditolak tidak disentuh, jadi satu laluan boleh menaikkan peringkat pada Gate yang mendapat manfaat dan membiarkan selebihnya pada peringkat pertama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A circuit holding both kinds of evolution shows what that saves. The predicate below accepts a gate only when its operator moves particles between modes, which is exactly when the groups fail to commute and a higher order has something to buy:\n"
msgstr "Litar yang mengandungi kedua-dua jenis evolusi menunjukkan apa yang dijimatkan. Predikat di bawah hanya menerima Gate apabila operatornya menggerakkan zarah antara mod, iaitu tepat apabila kumpulan tidak berkomut dan peringkat yang lebih tinggi mempunyai sesuatu untuk diperoleh:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The gates the filter saves are exactly the ones order two spent on the diagonal evolution, which the diagonal comparison above prices at eight (18 against 10). They bought nothing there, because that evolution is already exact at first order, so dropping them costs no accuracy.\n"
msgstr "Gate yang dijimatkan oleh penapis ialah tepat yang dibelanjakan oleh peringkat dua pada evolusi pepenjuru, yang dinilai oleh perbandingan pepenjuru di atas pada lapan (18 berbanding 10). Ia tidak memberi apa-apa di situ, kerana evolusi itu sudah tepat pada peringkat pertama, jadi membuangnya tidak menjejaskan ketepatan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Compare the two order-two circuits with each other, not against the unexpanded one. Leaving both gates unexpanded sends each to the fermion-to-qubit stage whole, which is the mistake the `apply=False` note above describes: it can land on the same entangling-gate count as the filtered circuit while being a different circuit at a different depth, so reading the filter’s benefit off that number measures nothing.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Bandingkan kedua-dua litar peringkat dua sesama sendiri, bukan dengan yang tidak dikembangkan. Membiarkan kedua-dua Gate tidak dikembangkan menghantar setiap satu ke peringkat fermion-ke-qubit secara keseluruhan, iaitu kesilapan yang diterangkan oleh nota `apply=False` di atas: ia boleh menghasilkan bilangan Gate berbelit yang sama dengan litar yang ditapis sedangkan ia litar yang berbeza pada kedalaman yang berbeza, jadi membaca faedah penapis daripada nombor itu tidak mengukur apa-apa.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Caution\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Neither knob verifies that the factors are Hermitian, and an incorrectly grouped operator can look *better* at an even order than at first order while still being wrong, because the symmetrization partially cancels the error. Group conjugate partners together, as `fermi_hubbard_chain` above does.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Caution\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Tiada satu pun kenop mengesahkan bahawa faktor adalah Hermitian, dan operator yang dikumpulkan dengan salah boleh kelihatan *lebih baik* pada peringkat genap berbanding peringkat pertama sedangkan masih salah, kerana simetrisasi membatalkan sebahagian ralat. Kumpulkan pasangan konjugat bersama, seperti yang dilakukan oleh `fermi_hubbard_chain` di atas.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah seterusnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation) for how the groups these product formulas split on are assigned.\n"
msgstr "Baca [Kumpulkan sebutan operator: gunakan struktur operator](grouping#grouping-explanation) untuk mengetahui cara kumpulan yang dipecahkan oleh formula hasil darab ini ditetapkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read [Transpile fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) for the stages a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") passes through.\n"
msgstr "Baca [Transpilasi litar fermionik](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) untuk peringkat yang dilalui oleh [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "See [Simulate 1D Fermi-Hubbard dynamics with flow sets](1-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) for a worked case where the fermionic formula supplies the step count that a custom qubit-side synthesis cannot.\n"
msgstr "Lihat [Simulasikan dinamik Fermi-Hubbard 1D dengan set aliran](1-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) untuk kes contoh di mana formula fermionik membekalkan bilangan langkah yang tidak dapat diberikan oleh sintesis sebelah qubit tersuai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consult [`synthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis\") for the synthesis methods themselves, and [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") for a randomized alternative.\n"
msgstr "Rujuk [`synthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis\") untuk kaedah sintesis itu sendiri, dan [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") untuk alternatif rawak.\n"
